--- !u!114 &1969420932
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1969420930}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<b> Cabbage Rolls (Latvian Style)</b>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<b>Ingredients
    (for ~10\u201312 rolls):</b>\n\nFor the rolls:\n\n- 1 large head of cabbage\n-
    800 g minced meat \n- 400\u2013500 g cooked rice (use more or less depending
    on how filling you want the rolls)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced\n- Salt & pepper\n-
    Oil for cooking (sunflower oil is traditional)\n\nFor the sauce:\n\n- 3 onions,
    finely chopped\n- 4 carrots, grated\n- Tomato paste or tomato sauce\n- 1\u20132
    bay leaves\n- Salt & pepper\n- Oil for cooking\n- Optional: heavy cream (not
    necessary if serving with sour cream)\n\n<b> Cooking Process </b>\n\n1. Cook
    the rice. Boil until done, then let it cool a bit so it\u2019s easier to mix
    with the meat.\n\n2. Prepare the cabbage leaves (and multitask). Clean the cabbage
    head; remove outer leaves that are rough or dirty. Place the whole head of cabbage
    in a large pot of salted boiling water. It takes a while for the leaves to soften
    enough to peel off. While the cabbage is boiling, prepare the filling (mix minced
    meat, garlic, salt, pepper, and rice in a bowl) and the sauce base (chop onions
    and grate carrots).\n\n3. Remove cabbage leaves. Once softened, carefully peel
    the soft leaves off, and let the ones after them soften as water does not penetrate
    the cabbage layers as well. Trim or flatten the thick stem so each leaf is easier
    to roll.\n\n4. Make the rolls.\nOn each cabbage leaf, place about 80 g of the
    meat & rice mixture.\nFold sides inward, then roll from the stem end until the
    filling is completely wrapped.\n\n5. Brown the rolls. Heat oil in a pan and fry
    the rolls until they start to crackle and pop, a pan lid should be used in this
    case. Flip the rolls once they are golden and a little overcooked for flavour.\n\n6.
    Make the sauce.\nIn a pan, saut\xE9 the onions, carrots, and bay leaf in oil.
    Season with salt and pepper.\nAdd tomato paste (or tomato sauce) and some water
    until the consistency is slightly thick but not watery.\n\n7. Cook the rolls.\nStovetop
    method: Place rolls in a pot, pour sauce over them, cover, and simmer on low
    heat for 45\u201360 minutes.\nOven method: Preheat oven to 175\u2013180 \xB0C.
    Place rolls in a deep baking dish, cover with sauce, and bake for 60\u201380
    minutes, until tender.\L\n8. Serve. Top with sour cream and fresh herbs (parsley
    or dill). Enjoy!\L"
